note right of IImageCropperFacility
  Implemented by the consuming project.
  The library decodes no image format
  of its own.
end note

note bottom of IADataExportersFacade
  The only entry point a consuming
  project needs. Everything else stays
  behind these abstract interfaces.
end note

note bottom of Ultralytics2FolderExporter
  One directory layout and one
  data.yaml descriptor; the label
  file line is what every YOLO
  task changes.
end note

note bottom of Coco2FolderExporter
  The one layout read by something
  other than a YOLO run, and the one
  carrying a rectangle in the image
  own pixels.
end note

note bottom of PascalVoc2FolderExporter
  One XML descriptor per image, the
  ones LabelImg writes and reads, and
  one of the two layouts naming a
  class instead of numbering it.
end note

note bottom of CreateML2FolderExporter
  Images and one annotations.json in
  one flat directory, the Create ML
  data source. The only layout whose
  x/y is the box centre in pixels.
end note

note bottom of ImageLoader
  Preloads the web hosted image
  records into a local cache before
  they are copied or cropped.
end note

